    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d783">

                <pb facs="1260" n="1164" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg1164"/>

                <head>No. 780.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Aristarchi Bey.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-07-28"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 28,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring again to your note of the 19th
                    March last, in relation to the measurement of vessels and tonnage dues on the
                    Suez Canal, I have the honor to inform you that it has been decided by the
                    Treasury Department to furnish vessels bound to Europe and likely to visit the
                    Suez Canal, a special certificate of admeasurement, conforming to the
                    international tonnage commission which recently sat at Constantinople.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH,</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
